    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. The advertisement promotes quick access to a cash advance, including an up-to-$250 framing, before the subscription, eligibility, and fee limits are known to the consumer.\nLEGAL REASONING. The complaint alleges Cleo represented that consumers would receive specific advance amounts or instant/today cash, when those representations were false, misleading, or unsubstantiated.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a).",
