    },
    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. The plan screen presents paid Plus and Builder subscriptions and preselects Plus, while cash-advance eligibility and amount remain unresolved.\nLEGAL REASONING. The complaint alleges Cleo generally withheld the actual advance amount until after consumers subscribed and paid, so the plan-selection screen is material to both subscription consent and the cash-advance representation.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(1)-(2), 15 U.S.C. 8403(1)-(2).",
      "container_path": "cases/cleo_ai.json",
