    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. The payment-review screens require subscription payment setup before Cleo reveals the actual advance amount the consumer can receive.\nLEGAL REASONING. The complaint alleges the flow collects subscription payment commitment first, then later discloses a materially lower advance amount, making the withheld eligibility information material to the subscription purchase.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(1)-(2), 15 U.S.C. 8403(1)-(2).",
      "container_path": "cases/cleo_ai.json",
